Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.4.8
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. Stage 1 fixes min_cells at
    300 and applies the same cell set before normalization and downstream
    metacell construction. Routing is resolved independently for every broad
    cell type. A cell type with at least two retained conditions uses the
    common-dictionary Pando condition-GRN procedure: candidate edges are
    discovered on the complete cell type and separately in every retained
    condition, exact TF-peak-target triples are unioned into one frozen
    dictionary, and every condition is refitted with the same unscaled Gaussian
    identity Pando interaction model. Only estimable coefficients with
    BH-adjusted P below 0.05, absolute TF-target correlation at least 0.05, and
    absolute coefficient at least 0.05 enter the regulatory penalty. A cell type
    with one retained condition uses the original standard Pando GRN and creates
    no condition coefficient. Stage 1 validates the required Pando API contract
    without imposing a package-version floor. Stage 1 automatically enables only
    the Pando arguments valid for each route and parallelizes independent broad-
    cell-type jobs without nested worker pools. Before outer parallel dispatch,
    bundled Pando motif matrices, regulatory regions and motif-to-TF mappings
    are materialized in the controller and passed to workers as ordinary
    objects. Parallel condition jobs retain one exact Pando object per cell type
    so local peak and motif feature spaces are never merged incorrectly; Layer 1
    routes each fit to its matching object. Paired-cell TF-by-ATAC regulatory
    effects are projected before exact SuperCell aggregation. Metacells use one
    multimodal WNN graph per broad cell type and remain condition-pure after
    membership splitting. Optional raw ATAC fragment files are aggregated to
    final metacell barcodes and recounted before metacell TF-IDF. RNA support,
    regulatory effects, GPR rules, cell-type-specific union GEM construction and
    directional penalties use consistent reaction ordering, bounds and medium
    scenarios. Stage 5 uses the original MATLAB CORDA2 algorithm from
    schultzdre/Constraint-Based-Modeling/CORDA2.m as the default
    context-specific completion after mapping cell-type multiome evidence to HC,
    MC, NC and OT reactions. FASTCORE and complete full-GEM scoring remain
    explicit supplementary routes.
    The adjustable original controls are MCxNCthresh, constraint, constrainby,
    om and ci under corda2_args. Actively reversible reactions are split once,
    the opposite directional copy is closed during each target assessment, and
    the original Step 1, Step 2.1, Step 2.2 and Step 3 dependency transitions
    are preserved. Directional targets are parallelized only within one CORDA2
    step from an immutable stage snapshot, then reduced in original target order
    before the next state transition. Cell-type-by-medium reconstructions run
    serially so each step can use the full Layer-2 worker budget; every step owns
    a fresh worker pool that is stopped and fully collected at its barrier. The
    completed structural models are reused by the primary and RNA-only scoring
    paths.
